1
00:00:55,911 --> 00:00:58,873
FILING FOR LOVE

2
00:02:29,880 --> 00:02:32,383
EPISODE 4:
PLAYING WITH FIRE

3
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:34,051
FRIENDSHIP BEYOND PARTNERSHIP

4
00:02:34,134 --> 00:02:37,888
James is an innovator
who greatly advanced AI technology.

5
00:02:38,597 --> 00:02:39,682
It took great effort to invite him.

6
00:02:39,848 --> 00:02:41,058
FUTURE OF HAEMU'S TECH INNOVATION

7
00:03:02,830 --> 00:03:04,540
Ms. Joo must be at work by now.

8
00:03:05,874 --> 00:03:07,251
Let's avoid her as best I can today.

9
00:03:19,138 --> 00:03:20,806
Mr. Noh, Good morning.

10
00:03:21,015 --> 00:03:22,766
How come we meet right here?

11
00:03:22,850 --> 00:03:24,101
It's a small company, isn't it?

12
00:03:24,852 --> 00:03:27,187
It's your lucky day.
I'll treat you to a coffee.

13
00:03:27,271 --> 00:03:29,607
- No, I don't want...
- What is it? An Americano? A latte?

14
00:03:30,107 --> 00:03:31,567
Are you a die-hard
iced Americano fan?

15
00:03:32,985 --> 00:03:33,986
I am.

16
00:03:35,613 --> 00:03:36,614
What?

17
00:03:42,036 --> 00:03:43,954
How can she be so nonchalant?

18
00:03:44,872 --> 00:03:46,165
She must've seen me.

19
00:04:01,722 --> 00:04:04,224
Yes. I have to stay calm.

20
00:04:05,434 --> 00:04:06,810
Act natural

21
00:04:08,270 --> 00:04:09,355
like I always have.

22
00:05:01,990 --> 00:05:03,200
That James guy.

23
00:05:03,701 --> 00:05:05,369
He enjoys the spotlight too much.

24
00:05:06,036 --> 00:05:08,789
I get that scouting him
is your greatest achievement yet...

25
00:05:09,206 --> 00:05:10,791
Let's focus on the sport.

26
00:05:19,258 --> 00:05:20,676
That was a close miss.

27
00:05:21,301 --> 00:05:23,762
You almost got the last one.

28
00:05:23,846 --> 00:05:27,307
I'm getting so old,
I can't even pull a trigger.

29
00:05:27,391 --> 00:05:28,892
The shotgun is pretty hefty.

30
00:05:29,226 --> 00:05:30,269
Shall we switch to a pistol?

31
00:05:30,352 --> 00:05:31,895
Hitting a target is no fun.

32
00:05:32,146 --> 00:05:33,897
There's no prey and it's still.

33
00:05:35,149 --> 00:05:37,317
You're a true sniper at heart,
Father.

34
00:05:38,902 --> 00:05:40,696
The day you first took me hunting.

35
00:05:41,572 --> 00:05:42,990
That's when I decided.

36
00:05:43,574 --> 00:05:45,325
That I would be a good, obedient boy

37
00:05:45,701 --> 00:05:46,827
because my father's scary.

38
00:05:49,037 --> 00:05:50,205
You cheeky monkey.

39
00:05:51,832 --> 00:05:53,125
Why don't you two have a shoot-off?

40
00:05:53,542 --> 00:05:54,710
It's been a while since I watched.

41
00:06:21,487 --> 00:06:23,697
- It must've been like war.
- It was.

42
00:06:24,114 --> 00:06:26,283
The staff got worried
they would shoot each other.

43
00:06:27,117 --> 00:06:30,245
It looks like the time has come
to make up our minds

44
00:06:30,913 --> 00:06:32,748
about which of the two
we should root for.

45
00:06:33,415 --> 00:06:35,459
Don't you think our fate

46
00:06:35,542 --> 00:06:38,086
depends on who Ms. Joo sides with?

47
00:06:38,170 --> 00:06:40,464
I don't think
Ms. Joo will take sides.

48
00:06:40,547 --> 00:06:41,715
She's straight as an arrow.

49
00:06:42,925 --> 00:06:44,009
Mr. Ahn.

50
00:06:44,426 --> 00:06:46,345
Yes, I'm coming, Ms. Joo.

51
00:06:56,438 --> 00:06:58,607
How can I act like nothing happened?
It's just not the same.

52
00:07:00,818 --> 00:07:03,320
What kind of art studio
has such flimsy security?

53
00:07:03,403 --> 00:07:04,530
If they teach a class like that

54
00:07:05,072 --> 00:07:07,282
shouldn't they at least
lock the doors?

55
00:07:10,494 --> 00:07:13,372
You're saying Haemu Electronics'
Junior Engineer Lim Ha-kyong's case

56
00:07:14,456 --> 00:07:17,334
will be investigated
separately by the research center?

57
00:07:17,751 --> 00:07:19,795
Yes, it's a simple case

58
00:07:20,170 --> 00:07:22,506
so the center's HR department
will investigate

59
00:07:22,589 --> 00:07:25,008
and all we have to do
is review the report.

60
00:07:27,010 --> 00:07:28,053
We'll take this case.

61
00:07:28,136 --> 00:07:29,555
- I'll come with you.
- Okay.

62
00:07:29,638 --> 00:07:30,639
No, wait, what?

63
00:07:31,223 --> 00:07:33,350
You'll go and investigate yourself?

64
00:07:33,433 --> 00:07:35,936
Yes, since the new CTO
James Lockett joined

65
00:07:36,019 --> 00:07:38,897
they renovated the interior
to give it a Silicon Valley feel.

66
00:07:39,690 --> 00:07:41,775
Let's take a day-trip
to get some air and look around.

67
00:07:42,025 --> 00:07:44,987
But I have
a one-on-one meeting today.

68
00:07:45,070 --> 00:07:46,405
Oh, do you?

69
00:07:47,447 --> 00:07:49,575
In that case...

70
00:07:51,201 --> 00:07:53,954
Who wants to go
to the research center with me?

71
00:07:58,417 --> 00:08:01,003
Teams One and Two are
mostly at other subsidiaries

72
00:08:01,086 --> 00:08:03,881
for the routine audit season,
so they have no manpower to spare.

73
00:08:03,964 --> 00:08:05,507
Yes, you're right.

74
00:08:06,592 --> 00:08:11,013
Then who wants to with me
from Team Three?

75
00:08:11,346 --> 00:08:14,016
I've been under a lot of stress
due to a chain of events

76
00:08:14,099 --> 00:08:15,767
and my bowels are acting up. Sorry.

77
00:08:16,727 --> 00:08:18,020
Oh, no. I must dash.

78
00:08:21,940 --> 00:08:23,650
Any volunteers?

79
00:08:39,416 --> 00:08:42,377
Jeez, this is driving me crazy.

80
00:08:44,171 --> 00:08:45,213
All right.

81
00:08:45,756 --> 00:08:47,758
I might as well face her head-on.

82
00:08:50,427 --> 00:08:53,263
- So...
- Isn't it a lovely day?

83
00:08:54,389 --> 00:08:55,891
Yes, but Ms. Joo...

84
00:08:55,974 --> 00:08:58,310
Shall we have some udon noodles
at the rest area later?

85
00:08:58,894 --> 00:09:01,146
There was one place
with an awesome broth.

86
00:09:01,229 --> 00:09:04,274
I think it was the rest area
with trampolines for kids.

87
00:09:04,733 --> 00:09:06,652
- Ms. Joo, about yesterday...
- No! Don't talk.

88
00:09:08,070 --> 00:09:10,989
I need to concentrate
when I'm driving.

89
00:09:11,281 --> 00:09:12,824
I can't multitask

90
00:09:12,908 --> 00:09:14,493
so I can't drive if you talk.

91
00:09:14,952 --> 00:09:15,953
Let's go in silence.

92
00:09:17,829 --> 00:09:19,915
- Still, I...
- I told you not to speak.

93
00:09:19,998 --> 00:09:22,250
See? I almost missed the exit.

94
00:09:24,544 --> 00:09:26,129
You do all the talking.

95
00:09:36,515 --> 00:09:38,850
You charged 57,250 won
on the company card

96
00:09:39,434 --> 00:09:40,727
and have four strikes
for poor attitude.

97
00:09:46,066 --> 00:09:47,567
Read it slowly and carefully.

98
00:09:48,527 --> 00:09:49,569
Okay.

99
00:09:50,278 --> 00:09:52,280
CONFIRMATION OF AUDIT: LIM HA-KYONG

100
00:09:52,364 --> 00:09:53,573
Who did you upset?

101
00:09:56,994 --> 00:09:59,913
- Pardon?
- You were obviously targeted.

102
00:10:00,664 --> 00:10:02,290
The personal charges
on your company card.

103
00:10:02,791 --> 00:10:04,501
That happened too long ago
to penalize you now.

104
00:10:04,793 --> 00:10:05,961
Being five to ten minutes late?

105
00:10:06,044 --> 00:10:07,629
You don't report someone
to the head office

106
00:10:08,046 --> 00:10:10,090
for poor work ethics
for going to a bank.

107
00:10:12,676 --> 00:10:15,429
Who did you mess with

108
00:10:16,888 --> 00:10:19,558
that a junior engineer
would become a target?

109
00:10:23,687 --> 00:10:25,063
The Audit Team is
an independent department.

110
00:10:25,439 --> 00:10:27,315
You can speak freely,
without any concerns.

111
00:10:27,816 --> 00:10:29,401
Your secrets are safe with us.

112
00:10:39,870 --> 00:10:41,538
Well, actually...

113
00:10:53,425 --> 00:10:55,010
I wanted to meet you, Ms. Joo.

114
00:11:03,518 --> 00:11:04,686
Ms. Joo, Ha-kyong...

115
00:11:09,608 --> 00:11:10,609
Let's get it done quickly.

116
00:11:27,918 --> 00:11:28,919
Let's sit.

117
00:11:35,634 --> 00:11:36,885
Would you like to continue

118
00:11:38,011 --> 00:11:39,012
what you were saying earlier?

119
00:11:40,472 --> 00:11:41,473
What?

120
00:11:45,018 --> 00:11:46,144
I have nothing else to say.

121
00:11:47,646 --> 00:11:50,357
I'll just admit
to all the wrongdoings.

122
00:12:02,410 --> 00:12:03,829
Your coffees are here.

123
00:12:03,912 --> 00:12:05,622
- Oh, great.
- Thanks so much.

124
00:12:05,705 --> 00:12:07,290
- A hot Americano, right?
- Yes, thanks.

125
00:12:07,374 --> 00:12:08,458
- Thank you.
- Have a snack.

126
00:12:08,542 --> 00:12:09,543
- Okay.
- Thank you.

127
00:12:09,626 --> 00:12:11,002
I shall try this one.

128
00:12:12,087 --> 00:12:14,005
- That tastes really good.
- It's the famous...

129
00:12:14,089 --> 00:12:15,257
- Mr. Sung?
- Yes?

130
00:12:15,340 --> 00:12:17,425
When will you give me
this quarter's expenditure list?

131
00:12:17,592 --> 00:12:18,677
Hae-young.

132
00:12:19,219 --> 00:12:20,595
Let us be. It's Children's Day.

133
00:12:20,887 --> 00:12:23,557
- "Children's Day"?
- When the Head of Audit's away.

134
00:12:24,349 --> 00:12:26,226
When the Head of Audit is away

135
00:12:26,309 --> 00:12:28,854
- The world is ours for the taking
- The world is ours for the taking

136
00:12:30,689 --> 00:12:33,150
Since Ms. Joo's out,
I plan to take the afternoon off.

137
00:12:33,608 --> 00:12:35,068
Hey, what's wrong with you?

138
00:12:36,111 --> 00:12:37,237
You saw what Ms. Yoon did.

139
00:12:37,487 --> 00:12:38,947
She took this afternoon off
then canceled it.

140
00:12:39,156 --> 00:12:41,241
You shouldn't use paid time off
when your boss is away.

141
00:12:43,118 --> 00:12:44,202
That's the truth.

142
00:12:44,369 --> 00:12:46,913
I see there's so much more
for me to learn.

143
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:50,959
- When do you need that by?
- Hello, everyone. Please excuse me.

144
00:12:51,293 --> 00:12:53,253
What brings you here,
Managing Director, sir?

145
00:12:54,129 --> 00:12:55,172
Oh, well...

146
00:12:55,922 --> 00:12:58,133
I should meet and greet
our Audit Team.

147
00:12:58,216 --> 00:12:59,426
You're pretty powerful people.

148
00:13:00,468 --> 00:13:03,263
Where's the star, Ms. Joo In-a?

149
00:13:03,346 --> 00:13:05,098
She's out of the office on business.

150
00:13:05,182 --> 00:13:06,308
It shouldn't take long.

151
00:13:06,391 --> 00:13:08,643
- She should be back today.
- Is that so?

152
00:13:09,811 --> 00:13:12,981
How about a team dinner
when Ms. Joo returns?

153
00:13:13,064 --> 00:13:14,649
It's gizzard shad season.

154
00:13:14,733 --> 00:13:16,818
Let's have some raw fish and soju.
It's my treat!

155
00:13:19,154 --> 00:13:22,741
- Mr. Jeon!
- Mr. Jeon!

156
00:13:22,824 --> 00:13:25,076
Okay. Text me
when you've made the reservation.

157
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:26,661
- Yes, sir! Thank you!
- Thank you!

158
00:13:26,745 --> 00:13:28,163
- Thank you!
- Bye. We love you!

159
00:13:28,246 --> 00:13:29,331
- Work hard!
- Yes, sir!

160
00:13:32,709 --> 00:13:34,085
I should've taken the afternoon off.

161
00:13:34,711 --> 00:13:37,964
This must be the first team dinner
since he came back.

162
00:13:38,131 --> 00:13:40,383
Ms. Joo doesn't need to pick sides.

163
00:13:40,467 --> 00:13:42,052
Her side came looking for her.

164
00:13:42,385 --> 00:13:44,221
- Good for her.
- I should report to Ms. Joo.

165
00:13:45,013 --> 00:13:46,848
- He's so tall.
- I'm excited.

166
00:13:53,313 --> 00:13:54,314
Ms. Lim.

167
00:13:59,903 --> 00:14:02,447
I got the impression
you didn't tell us the full story.

168
00:14:03,740 --> 00:14:05,325
If you feel uneasy talking at work

169
00:14:06,117 --> 00:14:07,327
do you want to talk elsewhere?

170
00:14:12,040 --> 00:14:13,625
There's a phrase
the Audit Team quotes often.

171
00:14:14,376 --> 00:14:16,169
"Police, prosecutor,
judge, and attorney."

172
00:14:17,504 --> 00:14:20,298
We investigate like the police,
prosecute like a prosecutor

173
00:14:20,382 --> 00:14:21,800
make a ruling like a judge

174
00:14:22,509 --> 00:14:24,344
and defend the whistleblower
like an attorney.

175
00:14:25,929 --> 00:14:28,139
If you wish to report something to us

176
00:14:29,099 --> 00:14:30,225
from that moment on

177
00:14:30,850 --> 00:14:32,978
we will act as your attorneys.

178
00:14:33,645 --> 00:14:34,688
So...

179
00:14:36,356 --> 00:14:37,357
You can trust us.

180
00:14:39,276 --> 00:14:40,652
But you're still Haemu employees.

181
00:14:41,861 --> 00:14:43,071
I was told the same last time.

182
00:14:43,321 --> 00:14:45,657
That I should trust you and tell all.

183
00:14:46,032 --> 00:14:47,117
What?

184
00:14:55,041 --> 00:14:56,084
Ms. Lim.

185
00:14:59,629 --> 00:15:02,090
- Hello, Mr. Moo.
- Is Ms. Joo there with you?

186
00:15:02,507 --> 00:15:03,633
She's not answering her phone.

187
00:15:04,050 --> 00:15:05,468
I'm not with her right now.

188
00:15:06,511 --> 00:15:07,971
I'll get back to you.

189
00:15:08,638 --> 00:15:09,681
Okay, bye.

190
00:15:10,432 --> 00:15:11,474
Mr. Noh!

191
00:15:12,350 --> 00:15:15,478
Get over here.
There are lots of interesting things.

192
00:15:26,698 --> 00:15:28,325
How did you make something like this?

193
00:15:33,538 --> 00:15:35,290
We suspect him, too.

194
00:15:35,373 --> 00:15:37,584
His mind works
on a whole other level.

195
00:15:37,667 --> 00:15:40,045
Right. He mastered Korean in no time.

196
00:15:40,128 --> 00:15:41,212
He's a genius.

197
00:15:42,297 --> 00:15:44,799
Don't you flatter me like that.

198
00:15:51,973 --> 00:15:53,141
Okay, because over here...

199
00:15:53,224 --> 00:15:54,809
Sudden team dinner
with Managing Director Jeon.

200
00:15:55,060 --> 00:15:56,311
Inform Ms. Joo for me.

201
00:15:56,394 --> 00:15:57,479
A 100,000-won bet.

202
00:15:57,812 --> 00:15:58,813
- How's that?
- Ms. Joo.

203
00:16:10,617 --> 00:16:11,743
- Deal.
- Deal.

204
00:16:15,413 --> 00:16:17,540
Mr. Lee Seung-hyun is on
a New York business trip to prepare

205
00:16:17,624 --> 00:16:18,958
for the unpacking later this year.

206
00:16:19,417 --> 00:16:21,127
PR Team's Managing Director
Cheon Joo-won

207
00:16:21,211 --> 00:16:23,046
is increasing contact
with the media to influence

208
00:16:23,129 --> 00:16:25,298
how they report
our management issues.

209
00:16:25,382 --> 00:16:26,841
We're keeping an eye on Choi Woo-tae

210
00:16:26,925 --> 00:16:28,551
Haemu Chemicals' Vice CEO
who was rumored

211
00:16:28,635 --> 00:16:30,220
to have received
a job offer from overseas.

212
00:16:30,804 --> 00:16:32,347
How are things
between Directors Ma and Han?

213
00:16:32,597 --> 00:16:34,682
They seemed to be fighting over
which accounting firm to hire.

214
00:16:34,849 --> 00:16:36,810
They seem to have
reached an agreement.

215
00:16:36,893 --> 00:16:39,020
The Planning Team
will report to you soon.

216
00:16:40,438 --> 00:16:43,691
Managing Director Jeon seems
to have stepped in as a mediator.

217
00:16:45,151 --> 00:16:46,236
Sung-yeol?

218
00:16:47,028 --> 00:16:51,616
Yes, he has been meeting
the main executives in turn.

219
00:16:53,785 --> 00:16:54,869
He's working hard.

220
00:16:55,453 --> 00:16:56,579
This evening

221
00:16:57,163 --> 00:16:58,706
he's joining the Audit Team dinner.

222
00:16:59,791 --> 00:17:00,875
The Audit Team?

223
00:17:01,376 --> 00:17:02,752
Gosh, I'm exhausted.

224
00:17:02,836 --> 00:17:03,962
Ms. Park.

225
00:17:04,045 --> 00:17:05,547
What brings you to this lowly place?

226
00:17:05,630 --> 00:17:06,631
Hello.

227
00:17:07,132 --> 00:17:10,677
The vice president will attend
your team dinner as well.

228
00:17:10,760 --> 00:17:13,179
- What?
- He can't eat raw food

229
00:17:13,263 --> 00:17:15,306
so you should book a barbecue place.

230
00:17:15,390 --> 00:17:18,184
Pick one with a decent wine stock.

231
00:17:18,518 --> 00:17:20,645
Email me when you've found a place.

232
00:17:20,937 --> 00:17:22,021
Bye, then.

233
00:17:22,730 --> 00:17:23,857
- Okay.
- Okay.

234
00:17:24,441 --> 00:17:25,525
Goodbye.

235
00:17:28,153 --> 00:17:31,406
Why are we
suddenly at the center of attention?

236
00:17:31,906 --> 00:17:34,117
Managing Director Jeon... Oh, right.

237
00:17:35,452 --> 00:17:37,662
We booked a raw fish place.

238
00:17:37,745 --> 00:17:39,456
The managing director
wanted gizzard shad.

239
00:17:39,539 --> 00:17:42,876
- This is a disaster.
- No, wait.

240
00:17:43,418 --> 00:17:45,503
Team Three is in charge
of the booking.

241
00:17:46,004 --> 00:17:47,755
They should decide.

242
00:17:54,387 --> 00:17:55,555
Okay, everyone.

243
00:17:56,097 --> 00:17:58,349
Is it that serious an issue?

244
00:17:59,100 --> 00:18:01,561
The managing director said
he wanted gizzard shad

245
00:18:01,811 --> 00:18:04,063
and the vice president
can't eat raw fish.

246
00:18:04,189 --> 00:18:06,399
What someone can't eat
takes precedent over want.

247
00:18:06,483 --> 00:18:07,650
Don't you agree?

248
00:18:07,984 --> 00:18:09,360
I'll book a barbecue restaurant.

249
00:18:13,823 --> 00:18:14,949
Sorry.

250
00:18:15,033 --> 00:18:16,910
It's not that simple an issue.

251
00:18:16,993 --> 00:18:20,580
Hae-young, don't you see
how serious this matter is?

252
00:18:20,663 --> 00:18:23,583
The Audit Team's fate
depends on this decision.

253
00:18:23,666 --> 00:18:25,543
You can't be so rash.

254
00:18:26,211 --> 00:18:27,712
The managing director was first.

255
00:18:28,630 --> 00:18:29,714
Shall we have fish?

256
00:18:30,507 --> 00:18:32,509
His was the prior engagement.
That's a decent excuse.

257
00:18:34,344 --> 00:18:36,721
But the vice president
is higher in rank.

258
00:18:36,804 --> 00:18:38,640
That might be viewed as insolence.

259
00:18:41,559 --> 00:18:43,019
It's the biggest crisis of my career.

260
00:18:43,603 --> 00:18:44,729
Oh, dear...

261
00:19:00,078 --> 00:19:01,955
What do you think you're doing?

262
00:19:02,497 --> 00:19:04,749
There's definitely more
to this incident.

263
00:19:05,583 --> 00:19:07,377
You suspected she was targeted, too.

264
00:19:08,670 --> 00:19:11,339
We need to look into it.
We can't waste time playing golf.

265
00:19:19,389 --> 00:19:22,100
Don't you see
how hard I'm working right now?

266
00:19:38,324 --> 00:19:40,618
- Hello, Mr. Moo.
- Didn't you get my text?

267
00:19:41,119 --> 00:19:42,579
Whether we should have
barbecue or raw fish.

268
00:19:42,662 --> 00:19:43,913
Get her to decide for us.

269
00:19:44,497 --> 00:19:46,124
What's keeping Ms. Joo so busy?

270
00:19:48,084 --> 00:19:49,168
She's currently taking part

271
00:19:50,628 --> 00:19:52,297
in a global competition.

272
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:54,882
What? She's doing a global what?

273
00:19:55,800 --> 00:19:57,594
Okay, fine. Bye.

274
00:19:58,428 --> 00:19:59,429
Oh, dear.

275
00:19:59,512 --> 00:20:00,513
Hasn't he asked her yet?

276
00:20:01,681 --> 00:20:03,182
We really need to make a booking now.

277
00:20:04,601 --> 00:20:06,853
This is so stressful.
What should we do?

278
00:20:09,939 --> 00:20:12,191
Look.
My hair's falling out from stress.

279
00:20:12,275 --> 00:20:13,776
What should I do now?

280
00:20:15,278 --> 00:20:18,156
Let's just eat both.

281
00:20:18,239 --> 00:20:19,240
Meat and raw fish.

282
00:20:19,616 --> 00:20:20,992
Are you suggesting a buffet?

283
00:20:21,075 --> 00:20:24,078
I looked them up,
and none of them serve both.

284
00:20:25,413 --> 00:20:26,456
You're wrong.

285
00:20:27,165 --> 00:20:29,167
The galbi place we had
last year's year-end party at.

286
00:20:29,917 --> 00:20:32,128
It's a barbecue restaurant,
but they also sell gizzard shad

287
00:20:32,211 --> 00:20:34,047
that the owner's mother-in-law
sends from Namhae.

288
00:20:34,505 --> 00:20:35,590
It's their seasonal offer.

289
00:20:36,716 --> 00:20:38,134
Hey, you're right.

290
00:20:38,217 --> 00:20:40,219
- Let me see.
- We found a place.

291
00:20:40,303 --> 00:20:41,304
Let me take a look.

292
00:20:41,387 --> 00:20:42,847
Why you... Take a look, sir.

293
00:20:44,349 --> 00:20:45,391
My word.

294
00:20:45,642 --> 00:20:47,101
Why are you sharing this now, Da-yae?

295
00:20:47,185 --> 00:20:48,936
You should've told us
before I started to lose hair.

296
00:20:55,943 --> 00:20:57,987
I had a great time, too, James.

297
00:20:58,488 --> 00:20:59,530
And also...

298
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:37,568
Ms. Joo, your driver for hire
will take you back to Seoul.

299
00:21:37,652 --> 00:21:38,736
- Thanks.
- Sure.

300
00:21:39,278 --> 00:21:40,988
- Shall we?
- In-a, visit again.

301
00:22:01,467 --> 00:22:02,468
Hurry and get in the car.

302
00:22:02,552 --> 00:22:03,553
Move it. Hurry.

303
00:22:04,095 --> 00:22:06,180
Sir. Follow the car up ahead.

304
00:22:06,681 --> 00:22:07,974
I'll pay you
double the fare to Seoul.

305
00:22:08,057 --> 00:22:09,225
- Okay.
- Wear your seat belt.

306
00:22:23,698 --> 00:22:25,450
I knew it.

307
00:22:26,868 --> 00:22:28,286
We're following James, aren't we?

308
00:22:28,703 --> 00:22:31,038
Will you tell me now
what we did all day long?

309
00:22:31,581 --> 00:22:33,708
You didn't do all that
to befriend him, did you?

310
00:22:34,959 --> 00:22:36,377
Earlier at the research center.

311
00:22:37,211 --> 00:22:40,047
I looked up
James' company card statement.

312
00:22:41,507 --> 00:22:43,843
The company
got him a room at the Baron Hotel

313
00:22:44,635 --> 00:22:47,180
but he's been frequenting
the Rosa Hotel.

314
00:22:48,014 --> 00:22:49,098
So what?

315
00:22:49,348 --> 00:22:51,017
Do you suspect James?

316
00:22:51,100 --> 00:22:52,643
I suspected him from the start.

317
00:22:53,352 --> 00:22:55,646
The target
was a young female researcher.

318
00:22:55,730 --> 00:22:56,731
But James is...

319
00:22:57,523 --> 00:23:00,026
You know,
even if he's involved somehow

320
00:23:00,485 --> 00:23:02,278
the higher-ups
will try to cover it up.

321
00:23:02,862 --> 00:23:04,238
If this backfires
due to a careless move

322
00:23:04,322 --> 00:23:05,907
you could be in serious trouble.

323
00:23:06,282 --> 00:23:07,325
Exactly.

324
00:23:09,410 --> 00:23:10,578
I'll make sure it doesn't backfire.

325
00:23:47,907 --> 00:23:48,950
Mr. Noh.

326
00:23:49,700 --> 00:23:51,369
- Run.
- What?

327
00:23:53,079 --> 00:23:54,330
We need his room number.

328
00:23:54,872 --> 00:23:55,915
Get to it.

329
00:24:00,628 --> 00:24:01,712
Hang on.

330
00:24:48,509 --> 00:24:49,594
He got into the elevator.

331
00:24:50,261 --> 00:24:51,262
What floor are you on?

332
00:24:53,389 --> 00:24:54,432
The fifth floor.

333
00:24:55,182 --> 00:24:56,267
Still?

334
00:24:56,684 --> 00:24:57,768
Run faster.

335
00:24:58,185 --> 00:24:59,228
Excuse me?

336
00:25:01,772 --> 00:25:03,190
Jeez.

337
00:25:14,452 --> 00:25:15,620
Nine, ten.

338
00:25:19,790 --> 00:25:22,627
It's 13.
He got off at the 13th floor.

339
00:25:47,068 --> 00:25:49,403
I saw him enter Room 1307.

340
00:25:51,572 --> 00:25:52,907
Babe.

341
00:25:54,408 --> 00:25:56,202
Come here. Hurry.

342
00:25:57,828 --> 00:25:59,038
Yes, over here.

343
00:26:02,458 --> 00:26:04,335
Look at you sweating.

344
00:26:05,294 --> 00:26:07,380
Did you run so we could meet sooner?

345
00:26:11,509 --> 00:26:13,719
Oh, yes, right, sweetie.

346
00:26:14,595 --> 00:26:15,805
It's so hot.

347
00:26:17,556 --> 00:26:20,351
You make a lovely couple.

348
00:26:21,018 --> 00:26:22,353
Which room would you like?

349
00:26:22,645 --> 00:26:26,148
We have rooms
with a city view, a park view...

350
00:26:26,232 --> 00:26:27,400
Room 1306, please.

351
00:26:28,150 --> 00:26:30,194
- Pardon?
- The thing is...

352
00:26:31,862 --> 00:26:33,614
We're celebrating a special day.

353
00:26:34,448 --> 00:26:37,702
We want to reminisce
on what we did in Room 1306 before.

354
00:26:40,705 --> 00:26:41,998
Give me a moment.

355
00:26:42,123 --> 00:26:43,374
- Okay.
- So that's it.

356
00:26:45,292 --> 00:26:47,962
Oh, dear. I'm terribly sorry.

357
00:26:48,045 --> 00:26:51,674
Someone already checked into 1306

358
00:26:51,757 --> 00:26:54,218
and the room next door, 1307

359
00:26:54,301 --> 00:26:57,596
just became unavailable.

360
00:26:57,680 --> 00:26:59,140
What about Room 1308?

361
00:26:59,932 --> 00:27:02,435
Oh, that room is available, but...

362
00:27:03,019 --> 00:27:05,021
Since you're celebrating
a special day

363
00:27:05,104 --> 00:27:07,690
how about we offer you
a free upgrade?

364
00:27:07,773 --> 00:27:09,942
We're very proud of our suite...

365
00:27:10,026 --> 00:27:12,236
No, we'll take Room 1308.

366
00:27:13,404 --> 00:27:16,449
Our suite offers a much better view

367
00:27:16,907 --> 00:27:18,659
- that I'm sure...
- We want to be...

368
00:27:21,537 --> 00:27:23,956
as close to the special room
as possible.

369
00:27:31,922 --> 00:27:33,090
Give us that room.

370
00:27:33,466 --> 00:27:35,760
It means more to us than a room.

371
00:27:38,012 --> 00:27:39,180
It's such a special memory.

372
00:27:40,639 --> 00:27:42,725
Okay. Oh, gosh...

373
00:27:43,142 --> 00:27:46,020
I'll help you check in
as soon as possible.

374
00:27:48,647 --> 00:27:49,690
It's this way.

375
00:28:06,207 --> 00:28:07,917
You put on a great show earlier.

376
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:09,335
Why are you hesitating now?

377
00:28:11,378 --> 00:28:12,463
You've already seen everything.

378
00:28:16,926 --> 00:28:18,094
Darn it.

379
00:28:45,496 --> 00:28:47,206
MOTHER-IN-LAW'S
SEASONAL GIZZARD SHAD FROM NAMHAE

380
00:28:50,835 --> 00:28:53,587
Shouldn't we seat the stepbrothers
across from each other?

381
00:28:53,921 --> 00:28:56,382
That will make this the top seat
and that would be weird.

382
00:28:56,590 --> 00:28:57,591
How about this layout?

383
00:28:57,842 --> 00:28:59,218
We separate the two tables

384
00:28:59,301 --> 00:29:01,512
so one has raw fish
and the other has barbecue.

385
00:29:01,595 --> 00:29:03,806
Wouldn't it be too obvious
that we separated them?

386
00:29:03,889 --> 00:29:04,890
- Right?
- Yes.

387
00:29:05,808 --> 00:29:07,143
This is a headache...

388
00:29:08,811 --> 00:29:10,354
You're here already.

389
00:29:10,855 --> 00:29:12,815
Hello and welcome, sir.

390
00:29:15,609 --> 00:29:18,863
Where should we seat you?

391
00:29:18,946 --> 00:29:20,489
Sit wherever you want, sir.

392
00:29:26,495 --> 00:29:28,205
What a bright idea
from our Gen Z employee.

393
00:29:36,046 --> 00:29:37,339
Okay. I'll sit here, then.

394
00:29:38,674 --> 00:29:39,884
Why not in the middle?

395
00:29:39,967 --> 00:29:42,595
No, this is fine.
I can see all of you from here.

396
00:29:42,678 --> 00:29:43,971
You can rotate after a while.

397
00:29:44,054 --> 00:29:45,139
Okay. We'll do that.

398
00:29:45,764 --> 00:29:46,974
The VP is here.

399
00:29:47,057 --> 00:29:48,267
- Hello, sir.
- Hello, sir.

400
00:29:48,350 --> 00:29:49,435
- Hello, sir.
- Hello, sir.

401
00:29:49,768 --> 00:29:52,980
What took you so long? I'm starving.

402
00:29:59,028 --> 00:30:00,571
- You can all sit down.
- Sure.

403
00:30:01,197 --> 00:30:02,531
Take a seat, everyone.

404
00:30:06,827 --> 00:30:07,870
Did I make you wait long?

405
00:30:07,953 --> 00:30:08,954
Gosh, no, sir.

406
00:30:09,038 --> 00:30:11,248
We just placed the order,
and they'll start serving.

407
00:30:11,665 --> 00:30:14,835
This is their wine list.
If there's anything you like...

408
00:30:14,919 --> 00:30:15,961
Jae-yeol.

409
00:30:16,253 --> 00:30:18,923
Don't drink wine. Soju is the drink
of choice for a team dinner.

410
00:30:19,006 --> 00:30:20,049
Aren't I right?

411
00:30:20,257 --> 00:30:22,176
Sure, soju sounds good.

412
00:30:22,259 --> 00:30:23,344
- Right?
- Yes.

413
00:30:25,429 --> 00:30:27,056
You can order whatever you like.

414
00:30:27,264 --> 00:30:28,265
Okay.

415
00:30:30,768 --> 00:30:32,228
I don't see Ms. Joo.

416
00:30:32,519 --> 00:30:34,355
Is she not back yet?

417
00:30:34,688 --> 00:30:36,398
Oh, I'll call and ask.

418
00:30:36,482 --> 00:30:38,275
- Call Mr. Noh.
- Okay.

419
00:30:38,651 --> 00:30:42,780
She's out on business
with Mr. Noh Ki-jun.

420
00:30:47,701 --> 00:30:48,786
It's so hot.

421
00:30:52,873 --> 00:30:54,375
Why are you undressing?

422
00:30:55,834 --> 00:30:58,295
I'm drenched in sweat
because you made me run the stairs

423
00:30:58,379 --> 00:30:59,713
to get the room number.

424
00:31:00,589 --> 00:31:01,674
So hot.

425
00:31:19,233 --> 00:31:21,110
- Hi, White Blood Cell.
- Mr. Noh.

426
00:31:21,193 --> 00:31:22,653
Are you with Ms. Joo?

427
00:31:25,406 --> 00:31:26,448
Yes, just a moment.

428
00:31:28,909 --> 00:31:30,035
It's Mr. Baek.

429
00:31:32,121 --> 00:31:34,081
- Yes, Mr. Baek?
- Ms. Joo.

430
00:31:34,498 --> 00:31:35,791
Where about are you?

431
00:31:36,125 --> 00:31:37,251
I'm in a hotel room.

432
00:31:39,253 --> 00:31:42,256
We're here for dinner
with the VP and MD.

433
00:31:42,339 --> 00:31:43,757
When can you get here?

434
00:31:43,841 --> 00:31:45,759
- I'm staying the night.
- What?

435
00:31:46,510 --> 00:31:48,762
- Pardon?
- Mr. Noh and I can't make it.

436
00:31:49,096 --> 00:31:51,265
- Send my regards to the bosses.
- Ms. Joo, it's...

437
00:31:52,224 --> 00:31:53,684
She hung up.

438
00:31:53,767 --> 00:31:54,977
What did she say?

439
00:31:56,061 --> 00:31:57,062
Well...

440
00:31:57,479 --> 00:32:01,525
Ms. Joo and Mr. Noh are in a hotel.

441
00:32:02,318 --> 00:32:04,737
They'll stay the night there.

442
00:32:06,447 --> 00:32:08,574
- Both of them?
- Yes.

443
00:32:11,660 --> 00:32:14,747
Ms. Joo, won't they get
the wrong idea if you say that?

444
00:32:16,498 --> 00:32:18,584
I couldn't say
we were spying on James.

445
00:32:19,251 --> 00:32:20,878
I only stated a fact.

446
00:32:21,253 --> 00:32:23,047
Yes, but still...

447
00:32:24,131 --> 00:32:25,132
Wait, I hear something.

448
00:32:27,885 --> 00:32:28,886
What's wrong?

449
00:32:34,558 --> 00:32:36,268
He's taking a shower.

450
00:32:36,769 --> 00:32:37,936
What?

451
00:32:38,020 --> 00:32:39,563
Okay, the rooms aren't soundproof.

452
00:32:40,064 --> 00:32:42,107
You can sit over here, Mr. Noh.

453
00:33:06,340 --> 00:33:07,466
Scoot over.

454
00:33:09,718 --> 00:33:11,845
You can't sit on a cold floor.

455
00:33:12,679 --> 00:33:13,680
Here you go.

456
00:33:31,323 --> 00:33:32,783
I'm so thirsty.

457
00:33:51,009 --> 00:33:52,219
This is a nice brand.

458
00:33:53,053 --> 00:33:54,930
I'll drink this
instead of getting paid extra.

459
00:33:55,556 --> 00:33:57,975
Are you really going to drink
in a hotel room?

460
00:33:59,059 --> 00:34:01,645
Yes, because I'm so thirsty,
all thanks to someone.

461
00:34:03,355 --> 00:34:05,732
What's wrong?
You said I've already seen it all.

462
00:34:20,289 --> 00:34:23,041
- That was delicious.
- It was so good. I'm full.

463
00:34:24,084 --> 00:34:25,377
Thank you for dinner, sir!

464
00:34:26,170 --> 00:34:28,213
- Thank you!
- Thank you, sir!

465
00:34:28,297 --> 00:34:29,715
- Hey, Min-su!
- Yes, sir!

466
00:34:30,090 --> 00:34:31,592
Let's play pool sometime soon.

467
00:34:31,675 --> 00:34:33,760
- Yes, and I won't let you win, sir.
- Please don't.

468
00:34:33,844 --> 00:34:36,138
Sir, you have to follow me back
on Instagram.

469
00:34:36,430 --> 00:34:38,432
Sure. No, while we're at it,
let me do it now.

470
00:34:38,515 --> 00:34:40,058
Really? Awesome!

471
00:34:40,142 --> 00:34:41,727
Sir, can you follow me, too?

472
00:34:41,810 --> 00:34:43,145
Wait a second.

473
00:34:43,729 --> 00:34:44,897
This is the kind of moment

474
00:34:46,064 --> 00:34:47,399
I really love.

475
00:34:49,067 --> 00:34:50,527
You're even funny!

476
00:34:50,611 --> 00:34:52,488
Follow me!

477
00:34:52,571 --> 00:34:54,323
Why don't we take a picture?

478
00:34:55,449 --> 00:34:57,242
- Get inside.
- Jump in!

479
00:34:57,326 --> 00:34:59,995
I'll take it now. One, two, three.

480
00:35:08,795 --> 00:35:10,214
- Mr. Choi.
- Yes?

481
00:35:10,297 --> 00:35:12,799
Let's stop by the pharmacy
for some headache pills.

482
00:35:12,883 --> 00:35:13,884
All right.

483
00:35:23,477 --> 00:35:24,728
I'll go and pick it up.

484
00:35:33,779 --> 00:35:35,030
What an immature day.

485
00:35:47,251 --> 00:35:48,335
Do I make you feel uncomfortable

486
00:35:49,711 --> 00:35:51,380
because of my feelings for you?

487
00:35:57,427 --> 00:35:58,512
Look at this right here.

488
00:35:59,888 --> 00:36:01,515
Park A-jeong.

489
00:36:02,266 --> 00:36:04,309
Your name is on the loan
as a guarantor.

490
00:36:04,768 --> 00:36:06,144
And there's your seal.

491
00:36:06,311 --> 00:36:07,688
I've never even seen this.

492
00:36:08,939 --> 00:36:10,315
This is a crime!

493
00:36:10,399 --> 00:36:12,276
Your older brother
is the one who conned us!

494
00:36:12,359 --> 00:36:15,654
The lease here and everything else
don't amount to half of what he owes!

495
00:36:16,363 --> 00:36:18,615
I gave him a good deal
because you had a good corporate job.

496
00:36:19,408 --> 00:36:21,118
Why don't you use this chance
to take on a new job?

497
00:36:21,994 --> 00:36:23,120
A pretty girl like you

498
00:36:23,203 --> 00:36:24,871
only needs a month
to pay back everything you owe.

499
00:36:44,099 --> 00:36:45,183
Mr. Vice President.

500
00:36:46,893 --> 00:36:47,894
Hello.

501
00:36:48,353 --> 00:36:49,730
My name is Park A-jeong

502
00:36:49,896 --> 00:36:51,898
the new executive assistant
from last week.

503
00:36:55,235 --> 00:36:57,362
I didn't expect you
to be at work this early.

504
00:36:57,446 --> 00:36:59,489
To be exact, I never went home.

505
00:37:00,907 --> 00:37:02,492
Why are you here already?

506
00:37:14,921 --> 00:37:17,966
I got this place
to occasionally spend time alone

507
00:37:19,635 --> 00:37:21,928
but I haven't had enough free time
to come here recently.

508
00:37:25,057 --> 00:37:26,808
Feel free to stick around
for as long as you want.

509
00:37:33,357 --> 00:37:35,192
I have most things you'll need.

510
00:37:37,944 --> 00:37:39,863
But there's no food or water.

511
00:37:46,995 --> 00:37:47,996
Do you want a drink?

512
00:38:07,933 --> 00:38:08,975
Have a seat.

513
00:38:14,898 --> 00:38:16,441
Let's skip this nonsense

514
00:38:17,275 --> 00:38:18,402
and cut to the chase.

515
00:38:19,111 --> 00:38:20,362
Do you want to shower first?

516
00:38:21,571 --> 00:38:22,823
Or should I wash up first?

517
00:38:25,242 --> 00:38:26,284
What's wrong?

518
00:38:27,953 --> 00:38:29,538
Are you into something specific?

519
00:38:52,853 --> 00:38:54,187
Just accept someone's kindness

520
00:38:58,316 --> 00:39:00,068
as kindness itself.

521
00:39:06,700 --> 00:39:08,118
If you think it's too much

522
00:39:09,453 --> 00:39:11,079
think of it as an employee benefit.

523
00:39:26,428 --> 00:39:29,389
Yes, the product is innovative.

524
00:39:29,848 --> 00:39:32,768
However, it's hard for me
to see the roadmap

525
00:39:32,851 --> 00:39:34,770
in the mid to long-term perspective.

526
00:39:36,646 --> 00:39:38,815
To include this in Haemu's portfolio

527
00:39:38,899 --> 00:39:40,484
not only do we need a good idea

528
00:39:40,859 --> 00:39:42,986
but we need to see
a specific execution plan.

529
00:39:44,863 --> 00:39:45,906
Yes.

530
00:39:47,115 --> 00:39:50,452
Yes, I'll check the vice president's
schedule and get back to you.

531
00:39:51,328 --> 00:39:52,370
Sure.

532
00:40:25,028 --> 00:40:26,154
I got a bit drunk.

533
00:40:27,989 --> 00:40:29,449
I have a question.

534
00:40:33,245 --> 00:40:34,788
What are you

535
00:40:35,413 --> 00:40:36,456
so tormented by?

536
00:40:37,457 --> 00:40:39,417
You never eat but only drink alcohol

537
00:40:39,876 --> 00:40:41,545
never sleep, and only work.

538
00:40:42,420 --> 00:40:44,130
If I were as rich as you

539
00:40:45,757 --> 00:40:47,884
I would only eat good food
and go out all the time.

540
00:41:08,280 --> 00:41:09,281
I know that was a mistake.

541
00:41:10,115 --> 00:41:11,324
It's late. You should go.

542
00:41:13,326 --> 00:41:14,578
It wasn't a mistake.

543
00:41:17,789 --> 00:41:19,040
I like you.

544
00:41:20,876 --> 00:41:21,918
Mr. Jeon.

545
00:41:22,794 --> 00:41:24,379
And it's not because I'm drunk.

546
00:41:24,963 --> 00:41:27,257
And no, it's not
because of what you have.

547
00:41:27,340 --> 00:41:28,633
I don't expect anything in return.

548
00:41:29,718 --> 00:41:31,261
I understand your situation

549
00:41:32,095 --> 00:41:33,388
and I already know my place.

550
00:41:35,390 --> 00:41:36,391
I just

551
00:41:38,852 --> 00:41:40,228
wanted to share

552
00:41:41,229 --> 00:41:42,230
how I felt.

553
00:41:44,900 --> 00:41:46,151
I'll pretend like I never heard it.

554
00:42:26,900 --> 00:42:28,068
What happened in the art class

555
00:42:29,986 --> 00:42:31,029
is more embarrassing for me.

556
00:42:33,615 --> 00:42:35,450
"Should I go and kill myself?"

557
00:42:36,868 --> 00:42:38,453
"No, should I kill Mr. Noh instead?"

558
00:42:39,579 --> 00:42:40,997
I went back and forth
millions of times.

559
00:42:43,041 --> 00:42:44,084
I knew it.

560
00:42:44,918 --> 00:42:47,045
- You were just acting chill.
- Yes.

561
00:42:51,383 --> 00:42:52,384
Jeez.

562
00:42:59,933 --> 00:43:01,226
I'm sorry, anyway.

563
00:43:02,435 --> 00:43:04,354
You must feel like you were violated.

564
00:43:04,980 --> 00:43:06,106
After all, I was the intruder.

565
00:43:08,191 --> 00:43:10,235
You had no idea when you came
to the art class, anyway.

566
00:43:11,027 --> 00:43:12,070
Sorry?

567
00:43:14,406 --> 00:43:16,116
Yes, right.
The recreational art class.

568
00:43:16,741 --> 00:43:18,576
Tell me about it.
What are the chances?

569
00:43:23,581 --> 00:43:26,084
Let me make this clear
in case you thought I had two jobs.

570
00:43:26,376 --> 00:43:27,585
I don't get paid to do that.

571
00:43:27,669 --> 00:43:29,254
It's like a hobby.

572
00:43:30,338 --> 00:43:31,631
Yes, sure.

573
00:43:32,257 --> 00:43:34,467
Something like a different job
didn't even cross my mind.

574
00:43:35,051 --> 00:43:36,302
I couldn't think in that situation.

575
00:43:46,980 --> 00:43:48,023
Anyway

576
00:43:49,983 --> 00:43:51,026
may I ask you this?

577
00:43:54,779 --> 00:43:55,947
Why did you take up that hobby?

578
00:44:01,369 --> 00:44:02,954
That way, I can breathe.

579
00:44:06,708 --> 00:44:07,792
I mean, you know.

580
00:44:08,251 --> 00:44:09,794
Every office worker
needs something like that.

581
00:44:09,878 --> 00:44:11,463
A place to breathe.

582
00:44:12,213 --> 00:44:13,256
That's why.

583
00:44:54,422 --> 00:44:55,423
But wait.

584
00:44:55,882 --> 00:44:56,883
How are your feet so tiny?

585
00:44:57,467 --> 00:44:59,052
What? My feet?

586
00:45:01,387 --> 00:45:02,680
No, yours are just huge.

587
00:45:04,808 --> 00:45:05,892
I don't think so.

588
00:45:32,127 --> 00:45:33,253
Could you stop staring at my body?

589
00:45:33,545 --> 00:45:34,587
What?

590
00:45:35,588 --> 00:45:36,923
Goodness, how can you say that?

591
00:45:38,508 --> 00:45:39,634
I also suffered

592
00:45:40,301 --> 00:45:42,220
from a great psychological shock!

593
00:45:43,346 --> 00:45:44,889
Are you saying my body was shocking?

594
00:45:45,056 --> 00:45:46,057
Yes, of course!

595
00:45:48,560 --> 00:45:49,853
No, wait.

596
00:45:50,270 --> 00:45:52,480
I don't mean that in a bad way.

597
00:45:52,564 --> 00:45:54,440
What I want to tell you is that

598
00:45:54,524 --> 00:45:56,860
- it was shocking in a good way...
- So you liked it?

599
00:45:57,902 --> 00:46:00,488
I mean, if I say I liked it

600
00:46:00,572 --> 00:46:02,323
it can lead
to another misunderstanding.

601
00:46:02,407 --> 00:46:03,908
What I want to say is this.

602
00:46:04,409 --> 00:46:06,077
What I meant was...

603
00:46:11,040 --> 00:46:13,168
So, now what? What do you want?

604
00:46:14,210 --> 00:46:16,546
Should I just strip naked right now?
That will be fair.

605
00:46:16,629 --> 00:46:18,131
- That's a great idea.
- What?

606
00:46:18,715 --> 00:46:19,799
Are you serious right now?

607
00:46:21,968 --> 00:46:24,095
Gosh, I can't deal with this.

608
00:46:25,388 --> 00:46:26,431
Watch out!

609
00:46:53,708 --> 00:46:54,792
Sorry?

610
00:47:55,728 --> 00:47:57,188
The Audit Team
from the head office is here.

611
00:47:59,899 --> 00:48:01,651
Why are you causing trouble
for everyone?

612
00:48:27,552 --> 00:48:29,762
You're breaking my heart.

613
00:48:30,805 --> 00:48:31,931
Don't be so uptight.

614
00:48:32,849 --> 00:48:34,100
No need to make a big deal out of it.

615
00:48:59,584 --> 00:49:03,171
Remember our forehead smack bet?
I won that bet.

616
00:49:03,796 --> 00:49:06,090
I wouldn't call that a smack.
That was a punch.

617
00:49:22,940 --> 00:49:24,525
He asked for a meeting.

618
00:49:26,152 --> 00:49:28,154
He had something to ask
about the research data.

619
00:49:29,989 --> 00:49:32,075
I was concerned
that it was held at a hotel.

620
00:49:33,159 --> 00:49:34,911
But that's where he had been staying

621
00:49:35,536 --> 00:49:36,746
and I heard

622
00:49:37,455 --> 00:49:38,915
he often held meetings there.

623
00:49:41,376 --> 00:49:42,710
It was my mistake.

624
00:49:42,919 --> 00:49:44,921
You didn't make a mistake, Ms. Lim.

625
00:49:45,463 --> 00:49:46,631
Please don't blame yourself.

626
00:49:49,884 --> 00:49:51,302
What are you going to do?

627
00:49:51,386 --> 00:49:53,179
We were really ordered to do this.

628
00:49:53,262 --> 00:49:54,305
We're unfairly blamed!

629
00:49:54,806 --> 00:49:57,266
It's James, Ms. Joo. James...

630
00:50:09,195 --> 00:50:11,322
- Thank you.
- You don't have to thank me.

631
00:50:11,406 --> 00:50:12,740
The Audit Team did what it had to do.

632
00:50:43,646 --> 00:50:44,856
She must be exhausted.

633
00:50:52,196 --> 00:50:55,199
QUICK CONTROL

634
00:51:16,012 --> 00:51:17,138
I have a question.

635
00:51:18,014 --> 00:51:19,849
During Mr. Son's infidelity case

636
00:51:20,224 --> 00:51:22,393
both Mr. Son
and Ms. Jeong were at fault

637
00:51:22,727 --> 00:51:24,479
but you only let Mr. Son stay
in the head office.

638
00:51:24,979 --> 00:51:27,315
- Yes.
- You said he was crucial to us.

639
00:51:28,483 --> 00:51:29,942
You said morals were different
in the office

640
00:51:30,026 --> 00:51:32,278
and we only had to care
about how it affects our company.

641
00:51:33,779 --> 00:51:36,741
But James is way more crucial
than Mr. Son.

642
00:51:37,450 --> 00:51:39,035
Why did you take things this far?

643
00:51:41,662 --> 00:51:42,747
Isn't it obvious?

644
00:51:43,623 --> 00:51:44,707
That was a crime.

645
00:51:51,005 --> 00:51:52,298
He's expecting you.

646
00:51:54,967 --> 00:51:57,178
You can wait here, Mr. Noh.
I'll report to him.

647
00:52:11,150 --> 00:52:13,653
You two must've grown close.

648
00:52:15,071 --> 00:52:18,533
I mean, you're standing here
like a puppy protecting its owner.

649
00:52:19,367 --> 00:52:20,910
You used to say
a lot of bad things about her.

650
00:52:21,327 --> 00:52:22,370
Are you picking a fight?

651
00:52:24,413 --> 00:52:25,498
I don't appreciate

652
00:52:26,249 --> 00:52:27,833
you staying the night out
without notice.

653
00:52:29,126 --> 00:52:32,129
Hey, I didn't stay the night out.
And that's my home.

654
00:53:50,458 --> 00:53:51,584
Hey, you're late.

655
00:53:51,834 --> 00:53:52,877
Do you want a drink?

656
00:54:00,009 --> 00:54:02,053
What's wrong with the vice president?

657
00:54:02,678 --> 00:54:04,180
He looked like a pretty chill guy.

658
00:54:05,556 --> 00:54:08,267
I've never seen him
like that, either.

659
00:54:09,310 --> 00:54:11,812
- It's James we're talking about.
- But still.

660
00:54:12,188 --> 00:54:13,898
He sexually assaulted
his junior staff member

661
00:54:13,981 --> 00:54:16,275
and even conducted a targeted audit
when she reported him.

662
00:54:16,359 --> 00:54:19,445
Who cares if he's James or Zeus?
We have to kick him out!

663
00:54:19,528 --> 00:54:20,988
Why are you so invested in this?

664
00:54:21,405 --> 00:54:23,866
You've never been interested
in justice.

665
00:54:24,784 --> 00:54:26,369
I'm not talking about justice.

666
00:54:26,744 --> 00:54:29,330
We're talking
about common sense, okay?

667
00:54:30,081 --> 00:54:32,333
Now that
we're talking about common sense...

668
00:54:34,251 --> 00:54:36,754
Last night,
what did you and Joo-In-a do

669
00:54:37,088 --> 00:54:39,965
all alone in that room

670
00:54:40,758 --> 00:54:42,051
throughout the night?

671
00:54:42,635 --> 00:54:43,803
What? What about it?

672
00:54:43,969 --> 00:54:45,471
I mean, it's common sense.

673
00:54:45,554 --> 00:54:48,057
A man and a woman
spent a night in a hotel room.

674
00:54:49,350 --> 00:54:50,434
Isn't that weird?

675
00:54:57,316 --> 00:54:59,193
Hey, we were there to work.
Can't you see?

676
00:54:59,527 --> 00:55:00,820
We caught a big fish like him.

677
00:55:00,903 --> 00:55:02,154
I'm sure you two worked.

678
00:55:02,446 --> 00:55:05,324
But did you spend
the entire time just working?

679
00:55:07,451 --> 00:55:09,203
So nothing happened?

680
00:55:14,500 --> 00:55:16,627
- Something happened.
- Nothing happened.

681
00:55:17,336 --> 00:55:20,631
I was stunned for a second
because your argument was so absurd.

682
00:55:23,884 --> 00:55:25,261
What's wrong with you?

683
00:55:26,887 --> 00:55:27,972
Wash up and go to sleep.

684
00:55:52,413 --> 00:55:54,206
Ms. Joo, the final report on James.

685
00:56:13,058 --> 00:56:14,268
Now, this one.

686
00:56:15,519 --> 00:56:18,022
Look at the scope of audit.

687
00:56:18,647 --> 00:56:19,690
Yes.

688
00:56:21,442 --> 00:56:22,610
Take a look at it.

689
00:56:34,038 --> 00:56:35,206
It looks good on you.

690
00:56:38,751 --> 00:56:39,835
Thank you for that.

691
00:57:22,545 --> 00:57:24,338
REPORTING MS. JOO IN-A

692
00:57:32,263 --> 00:57:33,848
SHE IS INVOLVED IN AN INAPPROPRIATE
WORKPLACE RELATIONSHIP

693
00:57:37,017 --> 00:57:38,269
I ATTACH THE EVIDENCE

694
00:58:16,473 --> 00:58:17,474
Mr. Noh.

695
00:58:20,019 --> 00:58:21,395
Are you not coming
to the class today?

696
00:58:21,729 --> 00:58:23,522
We're not doing quick sketches today.

697
00:58:25,774 --> 00:58:28,819
And I forgot to make myself clear.

698
00:58:29,486 --> 00:58:31,155
I don't mind having you there.

699
00:58:31,906 --> 00:58:33,532
Those classes happen
only from time to time

700
00:58:33,741 --> 00:58:35,701
and I can stop being the model.

701
00:58:37,119 --> 00:58:38,162
It's all right.

702
00:58:38,871 --> 00:58:41,582
It's fine by me, too.
Feel free to show up comfortably.

703
00:58:49,423 --> 00:58:50,674
I don't feel comfortable.

704
00:58:51,133 --> 00:58:52,343
And I have no reason to be there.

705
00:59:07,650 --> 00:59:08,692
Hey.

706
00:59:09,151 --> 00:59:11,111
You're not allowed to drink here.

707
00:59:11,195 --> 00:59:12,321
Don't be a nightmare.

708
00:59:13,322 --> 00:59:14,907
This is alcohol-free.

709
00:59:16,367 --> 00:59:18,702
Anyway, why are you here?

710
00:59:24,041 --> 00:59:25,042
No particular reason.

711
00:59:25,793 --> 00:59:27,086
I had no one to talk to.

712
00:59:27,252 --> 00:59:28,379
Don't you have any friends?

713
00:59:29,463 --> 00:59:30,589
Poor guy.

714
00:59:32,466 --> 00:59:33,509
Do you want to drink with me?

715
00:59:34,885 --> 00:59:36,553
Don't say something like that.

716
00:59:37,179 --> 00:59:38,555
Don't trust random guys out there

717
00:59:38,639 --> 00:59:40,057
and drink with them
like it's nothing.

718
00:59:40,224 --> 00:59:42,893
You need to be wary of them
and be cautious in this foreign land.

719
00:59:42,977 --> 00:59:44,103
Why are you taking this out on me?

720
00:59:44,186 --> 00:59:45,646
- What?
- Is your life in turmoil?

721
00:59:46,063 --> 00:59:47,106
What's with you?

722
00:59:47,523 --> 00:59:49,108
Have you still not found

723
00:59:49,566 --> 00:59:50,693
the pretty girl's man?

724
00:59:52,987 --> 00:59:54,613
I don't know who he is yet

725
00:59:56,448 --> 00:59:58,742
- but I've made progress.
- No way!

726
00:59:59,034 --> 01:00:00,244
Congrats, man.

727
01:00:00,744 --> 01:00:02,496
You said you had to find him

728
01:00:02,579 --> 01:00:04,081
to keep doing your job smoothly.

729
01:00:04,498 --> 01:00:05,624
Isn't that good news?

730
01:00:07,543 --> 01:00:08,585
It is.

731
01:00:09,920 --> 01:00:10,963
It's great for me.

732
01:00:11,046 --> 01:00:13,882
So why are you so annoyed?
It's great news.

733
01:00:16,885 --> 01:00:17,928
I wonder.

734
01:00:20,597 --> 01:00:22,391
Why am I so annoyed?
It's so annoying.

735
01:00:42,119 --> 01:00:43,120
Thank you for that.

736
01:04:41,191 --> 01:04:42,818
Have I always been this pretty?

737
01:04:44,987 --> 01:04:46,029
Right?

738
01:05:04,047 --> 01:05:05,048
You are pretty.

739
01:06:31,593 --> 01:06:34,513
FILING FOR LOVE

740
01:07:02,874 --> 01:07:04,876
A kiss definitely makes it official.

741
01:07:04,960 --> 01:07:05,961
I apologize.

742
01:07:06,044 --> 01:07:08,213
I shouldn't have done that
as your superior.

743
01:07:08,296 --> 01:07:10,340
- Like I was under a magic spell.
- Was she the only one who kissed?

744
01:07:10,424 --> 01:07:11,800
Why does she decide everything
on her own?

745
01:07:11,883 --> 01:07:13,051
Even after the kiss

746
01:07:13,135 --> 01:07:15,011
I thought an apology
would settle everything.

747
01:07:16,388 --> 01:07:18,181
I want to know

748
01:07:18,265 --> 01:07:19,474
if there's something more between us.

749
01:07:20,308 --> 01:07:21,309
Do you want to sleep with me?

750
01:07:21,518 --> 01:07:22,519
Do you?

751
01:07:24,146 --> 01:07:25,730
Can it really happen?

752
01:07:25,814 --> 01:07:26,982
Can you really fall for someone

753
01:07:27,816 --> 01:07:29,484
you've known for so long?

754
01:07:42,497 --> 01:07:44,499
Subtitles by Eunsook Youn
and Jennifer Lim

